    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0392" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg380"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.24/331</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Adviser on Political Relations</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Duggan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-02-17">February 17, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I telephoned Colonel Barber<anchor n="17" xml:id="d365-f1"/> and informed him of
                    the result of Mr. Welles’ conversation with Admiral Stark. He said that he would
                    put himself immediately in touch with Captain Spears and suggest to General
                    Marshall, as soon as Captain Spears receives his instructions, that the Army
                    representatives follow this same line.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laurence Duggan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d365-f1" n="17" xml:id="d365-f1-content">
                <p>Col. Henry A. Barber, War Plans Division, War Department General Staff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
